1lkt|n|of Prime ; The powder or other combustible used to communicate fire to a charge of gunpowder, as in a firearm. ; The first coating of color, size, or the like, laid on canvas, or on a building, or other surface. ; The carrying over of water, with the steam, from the boiler, as into the cylinder.	n:1d2v,41,3~1d2v,41,3	N:22xw,60,1~22xw,60,1
