1m36|a|Belonging to one; one's own; individual. ; Belonging to the natural or essential constitution; peculiar; not common; particular; as, every animal has his proper instincts and appetites. ; Befitting one's nature, qualities, etc.; suitable in all respect; appropriate; right; fit; decent; as, water is the proper element for fish; a proper dress. ; Becoming in appearance; well formed; handsome. ; Pertaining to one of a species, but not common to the whole; not appellative; -- opposed to common; as, a proper name; Dublin is the proper name of a city. ; Rightly so called; strictly considered; as, Greece proper; the garden proper. ; Represented in its natural color; -- said of any object used as a charge.	j:26xs,75,11;21dy,58,6;1egb,45,3;1bsr,44,4;33s,39,3;a6m,32,4;273t,30,3;1q4p,28,4;2881,20,5;3d4,19,6~26xs,75,11;3d4,19,6;21dy,58,6;2881,20,5;1q4p,28,4;a6m,32,4;2168,7,4;1bsr,44,4;1egb,45,3;33s,39,3
